<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Burgundian Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1477–1482</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Burgundian Succession was fought from 1477 to 1482 over the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, who died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI of France</a> seized the duchy of Burgundy and other lands, while Charles's daughter Mary and her husband Maximilian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> defended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> and won at Guinegate in 1479. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-arras-1482">Treaty of Arras</a> of 1482 divided the inheritance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-burgundian-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Burgundian Succession" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius (talk) 09:07, 5 September 2026 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte-Haus-Burgund-5-EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
